{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Everything is done and verified. Let me summarize the changes for the user.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"Everything is done and verified. Let me summarize the changes for the user.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"All done. I extended DSPy's media handling in `dspy/adapters/types/image.py` to support PDFs, videos, and arbitrary file types through the same interface that previously handled only images. Here's a summary:\n\n## Changes to `dspy/adapters/types/image.py`\n\n**MIME type detection via the standard library** (added `import mimetypes`):\n\n1. **`_encode_image_from_file`** — Reads any local file and determines its MIME type with `mimetypes.guess_type(file_path)` instead of naively building `data:image/{ext}`. PDFs now correctly produce `data:application/pdf;base64,...`, MP4s produce `data:video/mp4;base64,...`, etc. Raises `ValueError: Could not determine MIME type for file: {path}` when the type can't be detected.\n\n2. **`_encode_image_from_url`** — Downloads content and uses the `Content-Type` response header as the MIME type. If the header is missing, it falls back to URL-based MIME detection via `mimetypes.guess_type(url)`, raising `ValueError: Could not determine MIME type for URL: {url}` if both fail.\n\n3. **`_encode_pil_image`** — Uses the image's actual format and resolves the proper MIME type via `mimetypes.guess_type(f\"file.{ext}\")` rather than assuming a format, with a clear error if the format's MIME type is unknown.\n\n4. **`encode_image`** — Now accepts **any** data URI (`data:` prefix, not just `data:image/`), passing it through unchanged. Error messages updated to \"Unsupported file string\" for clarity.\n\n5. **`is_image`** — Recognizes any valid media file reference: any data URI, any local file path, PIL images, or URLs (backward compatible with all existing image handling).\n\nAll existing entry points (`dspy.Image`, `from_url`, `from_file`, `from_PIL`, `expand_image_tags`) work unchanged, so models like Gemini and Anthropic that accept non-image inputs can now receive PDFs/videos encoded through the same interface.\n\n## Tests (`tests/signatures/test_adapter_image.py`)\n\nAdded 4 tests covering: PDFs from URLs with a predictor end-to-end, multiple MIME types (PDF + JPEG), MIME detection from response headers, and PDFs loaded from disk.\n\n## Verification\n\n- All 19 tests in `test_adapter_image.py` pass (17 passed, 2 pre-existing xfails)\n- Full `tests/adapters/` + `tests/signatures/` suite: 56 passed, 2 xfailed — no regressions\n- Manual sanity checks confirmed correct encoding for PDF/MP4/MP3 files, non-image data URI pass-through, proper PIL MIME types, and clear `ValueError` messages for undetectable MIME types"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"harbor-endpoint","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":283,"output":611,"cacheRead":32896,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":15,"totalTokens":33790,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1788480541056,"responseId":"gen-1788480541-7yEgdqiwcfKGzRivT0Lg","rawStopReason":"stop"}}
{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Everything is done and verified. Let me summarize the changes for the user.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"Everything is done and verified. Let me summarize the changes for the user.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"All done. I extended DSPy's media handling in `dspy/adapters/types/image.py` to support PDFs, videos, and arbitrary file types through the same interface that previously handled only images. Here's a summary:\n\n## Changes to `dspy/adapters/types/image.py`\n\n**MIME type detection via the standard library** (added `import mimetypes`):\n\n1. **`_encode_image_from_file`** — Reads any local file and determines its MIME type with `mimetypes.guess_type(file_path)` instead of naively building `data:image/{ext}`. PDFs now correctly produce `data:application/pdf;base64,...`, MP4s produce `data:video/mp4;base64,...`, etc. Raises `ValueError: Could not determine MIME type for file: {path}` when the type can't be detected.\n\n2. **`_encode_image_from_url`** — Downloads content and uses the `Content-Type` response header as the MIME type. If the header is missing, it falls back to URL-based MIME detection via `mimetypes.guess_type(url)`, raising `ValueError: Could not determine MIME type for URL: {url}` if both fail.\n\n3. **`_encode_pil_image`** — Uses the image's actual format and resolves the proper MIME type via `mimetypes.guess_type(f\"file.{ext}\")` rather than assuming a format, with a clear error if the format's MIME type is unknown.\n\n4. **`encode_image`** — Now accepts **any** data URI (`data:` prefix, not just `data:image/`), passing it through unchanged. Error messages updated to \"Unsupported file string\" for clarity.\n\n5. **`is_image`** — Recognizes any valid media file reference: any data URI, any local file path, PIL images, or URLs (backward compatible with all existing image handling).\n\nAll existing entry points (`dspy.Image`, `from_url`, `from_file`, `from_PIL`, `expand_image_tags`) work unchanged, so models like Gemini and Anthropic that accept non-image inputs can now receive PDFs/videos encoded through the same interface.\n\n## Tests (`tests/signatures/test_adapter_image.py`)\n\nAdded 4 tests covering: PDFs from URLs with a predictor end-to-end, multiple MIME types (PDF + JPEG), MIME detection from response headers, and PDFs loaded from disk.\n\n## Verification\n\n- All 19 tests in `test_adapter_image.py` pass (17 passed, 2 pre-existing xfails)\n- Full `tests/adapters/` + `tests/signatures/` suite: 56 passed, 2 xfailed — no regressions\n- Manual sanity checks confirmed correct encoding for PDF/MP4/MP3 files, non-image data URI pass-through, proper PIL MIME types, and clear `ValueError` messages for undetectable MIME types"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"harbor-endpoint","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":283,"output":611,"cacheRead":32896,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":15,"totalTokens":33790,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1788480541056,"responseId":"gen-1788480541-7yEgdqiwcfKGzRivT0Lg","rawStopReason":"stop"},"toolResults":[]}
